{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/489896-cutting-off-body-parts","id":489896,"title":"Cutting off body parts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-23T15:31:32-07:00","id":489896,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Cutting off body parts","content":"I asked in the other thread, but I am not sure if many vampire people look over there.<br /> <br /> If you have a body part removed and you will it to stay like that, could you will it to grow back at a later time? Like you chop off a finger and years later youre thinking it would be nice to have it back? I know it's a super odd question....<br /> <br /> OR if you have your body altered with say a tattoo and will it to stay, would willing it to heal later make it go away?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T15:44:25-07:00","id":489924,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what the RAW interpretation would be, but to me that sounds like something the Ordo Dracul would have a rite for, provided you could pay their price of course","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T17:42:24-07:00","id":490088,"title":"","content":"I'd say you could repeat the expenditure to reverse the alteration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T22:10:06-07:00","id":490205,"title":"","content":"A more common example of this question is if Vampires could then spend willpower to regrow hair after they cut it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T22:42:35-07:00","id":490232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/489896-cutting-off-body-parts#post489896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked in the other thread, but I am not sure if many vampire people look over there.<br /> <br /> If you have a body part removed and you will it to stay like that, could you will it to grow back at a later time? Like you chop off a finger and years later youre thinking it would be nice to have it back? I know it's a super odd question....<br /> <br /> OR if you have your body altered with say a tattoo and will it to stay, would willing it to heal later make it go away?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, if you want to keep a wound, you can spend a point of Willpower before you go into Daysleep, and it will stay there afterward until you spend the Vitae to heal. Normally, this is a way to keep from coming up empty before you sleep so that you don't go into Torpor from healing. However, I see nothing wrong with having tattoos and other decorations 'permanently' emplaced by spending Willpower.<br /> <br /> I think at least one NPC in one of the books (Fall of the Camarilla?) is missing his eyes, and a related book (Requiem for Rome?) mentions that losing a limb or eye as part of a punishment should be kept, since healing the injury is taken to mean that you flaunt the authority of those who punished you.<br /> <br /> As for hair regrowth, I believe the mending takes care of that as you sleep overday anyway, while your body works to restore itself as it was at the point of Embrace. No Willpower or Vitae needed for minor things like that. (Though, I guess, if you got a sweet new haircut, you could spend Willpower to keep it in place indefinitely.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T04:00:20-07:00","id":490395,"title":"","content":"Right, all of that stuff reverts, unless you spend Willpower (point or dot, depending on the severity of the alteration) to keep it from mending. Vitalis was asking if you can later UNDO that change. <br /> <br /> So you spend WP to keep a tattoo, scar, wound, severed limb, whatever (this is covered in the book), but later want to lose the tattoo, heal the scar, regrow the severed limb, grow new hair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T04:46:09-07:00","id":490411,"title":"","content":"There's nothing that says the damage goes away, so I figure anything with an associated wound will be fixable. Anything that doesn't have one is a bit more permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T05:06:14-07:00","id":490417,"title":"","content":"That's a decent point; it's a change from 1e to 2nd that I hadn't twigged to yet. <br /> <br /> So for wounds dealing in actual Health damage you can prevent the wound from healing instinctively through daysleep by spending a point of WP per box of damage, but that leaves the wound permanently on your character until you spend Vitae to heal it. So you can leave your arm ending at a stump just below the elbow, but you're still going to have the damage that represents the injury. <br /> <br /> I stand by my previous assertion for reverting minor changes, like deciding you don't want a tattoo or scar anymore. Maybe 1 Vitae to &quot;heal&quot; all your cosmetic alterations, and a 1 WP point per individual alteration to seal it permanently. <br /> <br /> I could see a missing finger not taking up a box on the Health track (debatable, but I can see it) and being more cosmetic in nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T06:42:27-07:00","id":490468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/489896-cutting-off-body-parts?p=490417#post490417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I stand by my previous assertion for reverting minor changes, like deciding you don't want a tattoo or scar anymore. Maybe 1 Vitae to &quot;heal&quot; all your cosmetic alterations, and a 1 WP point per individual alteration to seal it permanently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is what I was discussing with my friend. Spend vitae to (undo) &quot;heal&quot; up the change they willed to stay would be a fair trade. Thanks for the input on this one guys.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T10:22:27-07:00","id":491736,"title":"","content":"It's not how this works. There are two different ways to spend WP to keep injuries. One's cosmetic (where you spend WP and Vitae ot heal the wound, so you heal up your health levels but remain with the cosmetic stuff) and the other ones is just WP where you prevent the wound from healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T10:25:00-07:00","id":491739,"title":"","content":"Can you find a reference for that, Griautis? I thought that was the case, but the bit I found didn't support healing the damage, but keeping the visible wound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T10:32:24-07:00","id":491741,"title":"","content":"Ah, I suppose the final paragraph of the &quot;The Cleansing&quot; section could be taken to mean that you can keep a visible gaping wound, or even a severed member, but heal the Health damage.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I didn't read it that way at first because it only references things like scars, tattoos and piercings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T13:26:40-07:00","id":491905,"title":"","content":"I'd personally rule that preventing healing and making a feature permanent are two totally different things for a vampire. The former is undone when you deliberately heal the wound. The latter never gets undone.<br /> <br /> I don't really think it's necessary or necessarily RAI (though I think it's certainly RAW), but I'd enforce it that way for thematic reasons. The physical stasis of a vampire's body is part of the theme. Being able to easily change and un-change kind of cheapens the effect and feels kind of silly, really. I see the unchanging undead form as one of the (minor) curses of being a vampire. If they can remove a tattoo they get bored of more easily than a mortal, this hinders that goal.<br /> <br /> Still, as I said, I'm not sure if that's RAI, and I certainly don't think it's the only way to do it. It's just how I'd do it, with my reasoning as to why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T07:12:05-07:00","id":492563,"title":"","content":"Tattoos are not that hard to remove. Flay the skin, heal, then use will to keep the change. Since the changes are retained through an effort of will, I say you can always revert back to your bodily appearance upon awakening after your embrace. You use the willpower and rest the same as if you were trying to keep a change. If you shaved your head and were embraced then you better buy a wig. However, if you were embraced and shaved after then you could go back even if you set the shaved head using willpower. You could &quot;naturally&quot; grow hair and nails using blush of life and and a daily dose of willpower, but that would take a really long time. That is just me though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T16:54:30-07:00","id":493012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/489896-cutting-off-body-parts?p=491905#post491905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really think it's necessary or necessarily RAI (though I think it's certainly RAW), but I'd enforce it that way for thematic reasons. The physical stasis of a vampire's body is part of the theme. Being able to easily change and un-change kind of cheapens the effect and feels kind of silly, really. I see the unchanging undead form as one of the (minor) curses of being a vampire. If they can remove a tattoo they get bored of more easily than a mortal, this hinders that goal. .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Another theme is that Vitae can do some crazy weird shit. And Actually a vampire could go get a different tattoo every night, and their body would just revert back to the time of embrace. so As it is written, they could easily change and unchange their bodies now. Same with a finger. could cut different ones off and regrow a new ones. If a vampire got surgery to get breast implants they could spend vitae to heal up weeks mortal healing in just seconds... Now... What happens if they dont will that to stay put as they slumber... Or What happens if they do will it to stay and then a few centuries later Fs arent in style anymore, could they will it back to their Bs or cut the change off and spend the vitae to heal to their original state of embrace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T06:46:59-07:00","id":493546,"title":"","content":"Well, at least for breast implant the issue is easy, for one they have to be replaced regularly, fun fact people don't generaly know but these things go bad. And if a vampire removed them and healed it wouldn't be a change, it's a foreign object, I highly doubt their body would sprout back a pair of silicone plastic wrapped bag the same way they don't regrow the clothes they were embraced in.<br /> <br /> In that line of thinking, maybe they could even get rid of tattoo easily as well, just strip the skin off and heal, maybe they will get a scar in the shape of the tattoo at worst, but I doubt they'd regrow the ink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}